    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363-a3">

                <pb facs="0734" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg624"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure B in inclosure
                    1.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cortina to Mr. King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-06-22"><hi rendition="#small-caps">June</hi> 22,
                        1889</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have the honor to call your
                    attention to the signature attached to page 15 of the documents in the case
                    against R. C. Work, as it is not the same that he employs in all his business
                    transactions; for, in place of being written as I have it above, with all the
                    requisite letters, it is written Wok; the same occurring in the marginal
                    signature. This can be proven by Antonio Doral and Severa Parkhini, who saw it
                    with me. And also it is not signed by his lawyer as are all the other
                    papers.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Cortina.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
